  "comment": "Glyph sets (docs/GLYPHS.md section 3). Pad families (`kind` pad, the default): the SVG of each physical control, named as PadControl in layer/sys/src/input_bindings.cpp (kPadNames), plus prompt-only names (diagonals, whole D-pad); faces are by position (on a Switch pad `south` is the button printed B). The keyboard family (`kind` keyboard): names exactly as the bindings file writes a source, `key:<name>` and `mouse:<name>` (the list is KEYBOARD_NAMES in tools/make_glyphs.py). A family takes the `shared` blocks it lists in `use`, in order, then its own `controls` (later entries win); `absent` lists the controls its device does not have. Edit, then run tools/make_glyphs.py.",
